 "the study was underpowered (minimum detectable effect 0.33pp vs observed 0.19pp; ratio 0.58)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["power", "minimum detectable effect"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 91, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[110, 110]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 92, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[111, 111]], "assertion": "point estimates ranged 0.16 to 0.29pp across six specifications, consistently positive", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["point estimates", "specifications"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [93]}, {"id": 93, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[111, 111]], "assertion": "only the continuous skin-tone specification reached statistical significance (p=0.042); the primary prespecified analysis did not", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["continuous skin tone", "p-value"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [92]}, {"id": 94, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[112, 112]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 95, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[113, 113]], "assertion": "even if accurate, the 0.21pp estimate represents an increase from 1.21% to 1.43% (~16% relative increase), a small absolute effect", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["risk difference", "baseline rate"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 96, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[114, 114]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 97, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[115, 115]], "assertion": "overall the evidence is suggestive but falls short of significance given p=0.148, wide CIs, limited power, and potential unmeasured confounding, so the hypothesis is not supported", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["p-value", "confidence interval", "power", "confounding"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 98, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[116, 118]], "note": "blank/separator/blank"}, {"id": 99, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[11